<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Mértola</h1><p class="st-meta">1033 CE – 1044 CE (approx.) · capital Mértola</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny taifa on the Guadiana at Mértola, an old river port in southern Portugal, independent for little more than a decade.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1033 a local leader, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tayfur">Ibn Tayfur</a>, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mertola">Mértola</a> and its district independent, in the period when the small principalities of the south-west were breaking away from both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudids</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-badajoz">Taifa of Badajoz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief references in Arabic chronicles, the state consisted of the hilltop town and its castle above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a>, the highest navigable point for river traffic from the Atlantic, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> and grain trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1044 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid-of-seville">al-Mutadid</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-seville">Taifa of Seville</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mertola">Mértola</a>. A century later it became the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a>, as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-taifa-of-mertola">Second Taifa of Mértola</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-mertola.jpg" alt="Taifa of Mértola" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_M%C3%A9rtola.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1033 CE – 1044 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mértola</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ibn Tayfur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Portugal</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Mértola</dd></dl></aside></div>

